{{ img:units/Mine.png|Mine}}
=Mine=
*  Health: 8
*  Price: %Minerals% 40
*  [[concepts/scanning range|Scanning range]]: 2
*  Consumes: %Energy%10
*  Storage capacity: %Minerals%10
Storage structures accumulate excess production of the respective [[concepts/resources]] from the local [[concepts/compound]] until they are full. Disabling a storage structure will change its priority such, that excess [[concepts/resources]] are stored here only if all other storage capacities are exhausted. Likewise, resource demand will remove [[concepts/resources]] from disabled storage structures first, such that they tend towards empty. Storage structures do not require %Energy% to operate.
Enabled mines extract any natural [[concepts/resources]] available in the planet-core beneath their location. They are essential in supplying other structures of the local [[concepts/compound]]. Mines should be build only on known occurrences of natural [[concepts/resources]]. They cannot be constructed atop each other, since they require a working link to the planet core in order to operate. Mines, like many structures, require %Energy% from [[units/structures/generator]]s to operate.
